# North Wind Avatar's trigger does not need the Avatar to stay (CR 113.7a): with the trigger on the stack Bot2 returns the Avatar
# to Bot1's hand with Bounce Off, and the trigger still resolves - "if you cast it" was true as it triggered and stays true, since
# the spell was cast (CR 603.4). Bot1 takes Counterspell from its sideboard. Its hand ends with the Avatar and Counterspell.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
North Wind Avatar
Island
Island
Island x10

[Bot1 Sideboard]
Lightning Bolt
Counterspell

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Bounce Off
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.North Wind Avatar.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Bounce Off.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.North Wind Avatar)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Hand.North Wind Avatar.Power = 5
Bot1.Choose(Counterspell)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 4
Bot1.Hand = Island; Island; North Wind Avatar; Counterspell
Bot1.Sideboard = Lightning Bolt
Bot2.Graveyard = Bounce Off
